---
import { TRUST_BENEFITS } from '../../lib/home';
---

<section class="not-prose">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 py-12 sm:px-6 md:py-16 lg:py-20">
    <div class="grid items-start gap-10 lg:grid-cols-12">
      <div class="lg:col-span-6">
        <h2 class="font-heading mb-6 text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900 sm:text-4xl dark:text-white">
          You shouldn't have to become an immigration expert just to understand your options.
        </h2>
        <p class="mb-4 text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted dark:text-slate-400">
          Different countries have different rules. Different pathways require different documents. And one missing
          detail can create unnecessary confusion.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-6 text-lg font-medium text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200">That's where we come in.</p>
        <p class="rounded-lg border border-primary/20 bg-primary/5 px-4 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:border-primary/30 dark:bg-primary/10 dark:text-slate-100">
          We will never tell you something is guaranteed when it isn't.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="lg:col-span-6">
        <ul class="rounded-lg border border-gray-200 bg-white p-6 shadow-none dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900">
          {TRUST_BENEFITS.map((item) => (
            <li class="flex gap-3 border-b border-gray-100 py-3 last:border-0 last:pb-0 first:pt-0 dark:border-slate-800">
              <span class="mt-0.5 text-primary" aria-hidden="true">✓</span>
              <span class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">{item}</span>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
